    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Promoting academic integrity is vital. Educators should provide clear guidelines on student responsibilities, emphasizing trust and dialogue. Evaluation methods should include authentic, varied assessments, which deter cheating. Collaboration boundaries must be transparent, outlining the scope of external help and proper citation requirements. Cheating or plagiarizing results in zero scores, with repeated offenses leading to disciplinary actions. Originality is paramount; submitted work should be distinct and honest. Plagiarism is not only a breach of trust but equates to intellectual theft. For a genuine academic journey, students must prioritize originality and understand its critical importance.</div>\n",
